# Instagram-ready Jekyll posts

Every `_posts` entry is published to `/feed.xml` and picked up by Make.com (`us2.make.com`) for Instagram. Missing `image`/`tags` or a non-JPEG outside Instagram’s ratio will fail that scenario.

## Required front matter

```yaml
layout: post
title: "Short readable title"
date: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS -0700
categories: news
tags:
  - news
  - topic-word
image: /assets/images/posts/slug.jpg
```

- `image` must be a **JPEG** under `assets/images/posts/` (`.jpg`).
- The **same file** must be the photo shown in the post body. Make does not convert or crop; Instagram gets this URL as-is.
- `tags` must include `news` plus at least one topic tag (feeds + Make filters).

## Image specs (Instagram photo post)

| Rule | Value |
|---|---|
| Type | JPEG only (convert PNG/WebP/HEIC) |
| Width | 1080px preferred (320–1440) |
| Ratio width/height | **0.8–1.91** (4:5 to 1.91:1) |
| Safe targets | **1080×1350** (4:5) or **1080×1080** (1:1) |

If the source is too tall (for example 2:3), **crop** to 4:5 from the center, then resize. Do not letterbox. Keep the original for on-page display if needed; `image:` must point at the converted file.

## Convert locally

Use PowerShell `System.Drawing` or `magick`. Save as JPEG quality 90. Example target: `assets/images/posts/2026-08-28-new-website.jpg`.

After converting, confirm ratio is between 0.8 and 1.91 and the path in `image:` matches the file.

## Do not

- Point `image:` at a relative HTML-only `<img>`, a PNG, or a PhotoPrism URL.
- Use portrait crops taller than 4:5.
- Skip `tags` or `image` on a news post.
